        "5CZbdNRyhlHPkTZYsbxs-"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8ZM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 13144409,
      "version": 218,
      "versionNonce": 25000281,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "8P6sCRkx6N0VjLUuJfzPi",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1754109714435,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "First Fully Connected (Dense) Layer\n\nWhat’s happening: A fully connected layer (nn.Linear) is defined that takes an input of size 768 and\noutputs a size of 512.\nWhy:\n\nThe input size 768 matches the hidden size of BERT’s output embeddings (for models like bert-base-\nuncased, which has 768-dimensional hidden states).\nThis layer reduces the dimensionality from 768 to 512, acting as a bottleneck to extract more task-\nspecific features from BERT’s general-purpose embeddings.\nIt’s a linear transformation: output = input @ weight.T + bias, where @ is matrix multiplication.\n\n\nKey point: This layer projects BERT’s high-dimensional output into a smaller space, preparing it for\nfurther processing",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "First Fully Connected (Dense) Layer\n\nWhat’s happening: A fully connected layer (nn.Linear) is defined that takes an input of size 768 and outputs a size of 512.\nWhy:\n\nThe input size 768 matches the hidden size of BERT’s output embeddings (for models like bert-base-uncased, which has 768-dimensional hidden states).\nThis layer reduces the dimensionality from 768 to 512, acting as a bottleneck to extract more task-specific features from BERT’s general-purpose embeddings.\nIt’s a linear transformation: output = input @ weight.T + bias, where @ is matrix multiplication.\n\n\nKey point: This layer projects BERT’s high-dimensional output into a smaller space, preparing it for further processing",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
