      "height": 630,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "OkPXles8-Y6gYqEMfnr4z"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8u",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1682590393,
      "version": 89,
      "versionNonce": 235370521,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1754109711363,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\nNature of Classification Tasks:\n\nText Classification: Spam classification involves assigning a label (spam or non-spam) to a text input,\nrequiring the model to understand the semantic content of the text.\nEncoder-Only Suitability: Encoder-only models like BERT are designed to generate rich, contextual\nrepresentations of text, ideal for tasks where the entire input sequence needs to be understood to make a\nsingle prediction.\n\n\nBERT’s Architecture:\n\nBidirectional Encoding: BERT, an encoder-only transformer, processes the entire input sequence\nbidirectionally, capturing context from both left and right of each token.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\nNature of Classification Tasks:\n\nText Classification: Spam classification involves assigning a label (spam or non-spam) to a text input, requiring the model to understand the semantic content of the text.\nEncoder-Only Suitability: Encoder-only models like BERT are designed to generate rich, contextual representations of text, ideal for tasks where the entire input sequence needs to be understood to make a single prediction.\n\n\nBERT’s Architecture:\n\nBidirectional Encoding: BERT, an encoder-only transformer, processes the entire input sequence bidirectionally, capturing context from both left and right of each token.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TYp1shJbGdgSJLRMzZzbi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12812.397178578467,
      "y": 12787.247725887124,
      "width": 1355.2651570638031,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "OkPXles8-Y6gYqEMfnr4z"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8v",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 761596153,
      "version": 75,
      "versionNonce": 1381921271,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1754109711363,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why Use an Encoder-Only Model for Classification",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why Use an Encoder-Only Model for Classification",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "yZW5P9H-TlYteTYcuxPHQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 12778.696494984717,
      "y": 14424.247720800859,
      "width": 1897.5527750651042,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "OkPXles8-Y6gYqEMfnr4z"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8w",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 984307095,
      "version": 109,
      "versionNonce": 1584598265,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1754109711363,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why Not Decoder or Encoder-Decoder Models:\n\nDecoder Models: Designed for generative tasks (e.g., text generation, as in GPT), decoders focus on\npredicting the next token, not summarizing entire inputs for classification.\nEncoder-Decoder Models: Suited for sequence-to-sequence tasks (e.g., translation, summarization, as in T5\nor BART), where both input and output sequences are processed. For classification, only the input needs\nencoding, making encoder-only models more efficient.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why Not Decoder or Encoder-Decoder Models:\n\nDecoder Models: Designed for generative tasks (e.g., text generation, as in GPT), decoders focus on predicting the next token, not summarizing entire inputs for classification.\nEncoder-Decoder Models: Suited for sequence-to-sequence tasks (e.g., translation, summarization, as in T5 or BART), where both input and output sequences are processed. For classification, only the input needs encoding, making encoder-only models more efficient.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jkP9Ekc3Q_p9w9Gkhgjsg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11936.133520266823,
      "y": 15813.525403635043,
      "width": 795.3477783203125,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "w7rVj8S1AuJFgqOoXErso"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b8x",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 482687417,
      "version": 56,
      "versionNonce": 1838426263,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "W1jUtiZXE0OULYlwTeumB",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1754109831561,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We can add multiple linear layers (e.g., nn.Linear(768, 512), nn.Linear(512, 256),\nnn.Linear(256, number_of_classes)) with non-linear activation functions (ReLU,\netc.) and dropout between them if desired.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We can add multiple linear layers (e.g., nn.Linear(768, 512), nn.Linear(512, 256), nn.Linear(256, number_of_classes)) with non-linear activation functions (ReLU, etc.) and dropout between them if desired.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
